Don't worry, these are two very solvable problems.

    Cursor Issue: The "missing cursor" happens because your index.html forces cursor: none (for the custom cursor effect), but on the Login page, we hide the custom cursor... leaving you with no cursor at all. We will fix this by forcing the cursor back to "Auto" on admin pages.

    Persistence Issue: Your Admin Dashboard is hardcoded to update ID: 1. If your database (after the reset) created a row with ID: 2 or ID: 5 (which happens with auto-incrementing IDs), your "Save" button updates a row that doesn't exist. We will make the code smart enough to find the correct ID automatically.

Here is the code to fix both issues permanently.
